---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="About Jason Marsh - Director of Technology specializing in assistive technology and AI engineering.">
  <div class="prose about-prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <img src="/jason.jpg" alt="Jason Marsh, headshot portrait" class="about-photo" width="240" height="240" />
    <p>
      I'm Jason - Director of Technology at an assistive technology & older adult services nonprofit in
      Duluth, Minnesota, with 13+ years in IT. I manage infrastructure, lead assistive
      technology services, and run an AT lending library. The people we serve are older
      adults, people with disabilities, and anyone who needs help navigating technology.
      I hold an Assistive Technology Applications Certificate from CSUN.
    </p>

    <p>
      I also build and maintain production software outside of that role.
      <a href="/projects/mealdeck/">A meal planning app</a> with AI-powered
      recipe adaptation. <a href="/projects/whatcanhelp/">An AT discovery tool</a>
      that matches people with assistive technology.
      <a href="/projects/petfeedr/">An automated pet feeder</a>
      on a Raspberry Pi. <a href="/projects/radiogridxl/">A radio streaming app</a>
      built for accessibility and deployed to older adults at my organization.
      <a href="/projects/echoetcher/">A voice-to-notes pipeline</a> that turns
      spoken memos into structured Markdown. Node.js, SQLite, and vanilla JavaScript
      for most of it, Python for machine learning and automation.
    </p>

    <p>
      I've been fascinated with computers since I was a kid - learned to fix them
      because I broke them. Art and design started in my teens, which led to a
      B.S. in Game Art & Design, then time as a concept artist doing noir-style
      western illustrations. Software came through years of self-teaching after
      that. The whole path still shapes how I work: I think visually, I design
      for the person using the thing, and I see projects through from architecture
      to interface.
    </p>

    <p>
      For a more detailed look at my experience and skills, check out my <a href="/resume/">resume</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How I build</h2>

    <p>
      I orchestrate, AI implements. Most of what's here - the production apps, this site, the
      project pages - I build by working through <a href="https://claude.com/product/claude-code">Claude Code</a> in
      the terminal: I make the calls on architecture, design, and tradeoffs, and the
      implementation happens in conversation. It's a tool, not a co-author. <a href="/oak/">More on how the site is built.</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>

    <p>
      I'm interested in AI engineering, assistive technology, and the places they
      overlap. If something here catches your attention, reach out.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Email: <a href="mailto:regularlyjason@icloud.com">regularlyjason@icloud.com</a></li>
      <li>LinkedIn: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jason-marsh">jason-marsh</a></li>
      <li>GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/Minimalistic">Minimalistic</a></li>
      <li>Art: <a href="https://jasonhmarsh.artstation.com">ArtStation</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* magazine-style wrap: text flows to the right of the photo and continues
     below it with the same visual gap on all sides */
  .about-prose .about-photo {
    float: left;
    width: 240px;
    height: 240px;
    margin: 0.35rem 1.75rem 1rem 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    object-fit: cover;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    shape-outside: inset(0 round var(--radius-lg));
  }
  .about-prose p {
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  /* clear the float before the h2 so "Get in touch" never sits beside the photo */
  .about-prose h2 {
    clear: left;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .about-prose .about-photo {
      float: none;
      display: block;
      width: 160px;
      height: 160px;
      margin: 0 auto 1.25rem;
    }
  }
</style>
